menu "OTA update"

config OTA_ERASE_NVS_ON_BOOT
    bool "Erase NVS + storage on first boot after OTA"
    default n
    help
        When enabled, the first boot after a successful OTA (image
        pending verify) erases the nvs and storage partitions before
        connecting. The device then enters Wi-Fi provisioning (AP
        SireneValidator). Disable for normal production OTA updates.

config SIRENE_OTA_REQUIRE_HTTPS
    bool "Require HTTPS URLs for OTA_UPDATE command"
    default y
    help
        Rejects http:// OTA URLs from MQTT. LAN HTTP OTA still possible
        when disabled (e.g. development). Secure Boot signing is a
        separate manufacturing step — enable via ESP-IDF Secure Boot
        menu when the signing pipeline is ready.

endmenu
